    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://www.osm.ca/app/uploads/2025/12/osm2526_dubois_1080x1080_bilingue-1.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://www.osm.ca/en/concert/dubois-biographie-symphonique/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/performer": [
      {
        "@id": "_:g1370760"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://www.osm.ca/en/concert/dubois-biographie-symphonique/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Dubois – Biographie symphonique"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<p>A passionate artist, Claude Dubois has always sung our stories, our loves, and our joys. With <strong><em>Dubois Biographie symphonique</em></strong>, <strong>GSI Musique</strong> offers a creation in the artist’s image—free and vibrant—where each note becomes a memory and paints the portrait of an artist who continues to move and inspire. The result of many months of work, the singer-songwriter wished to offer an exclusively instrumental production as grand and memorable as the many songs he has shared with his audience throughout his prolific career.</p>\n<p>From <em>Comme un million de gens</em> to <em>Si Dieu existe</em>, each piece—performed without lyrics and carried by <strong>Scott Price</strong>’s orchestrations—reveals all the melodic richness and emotional depth of a repertoire firmly anchored in the collective memory. This symphonic concert is performed by l’<strong>Orchestre symphonique de Montréal</strong> and conducted by maestro <strong>Dina Gilbert</strong>.</p>\n"
      }
    ]
  },
