      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "The novel Corinne ou l’Italie by Madame de Staël depicts various regions of the country while offering thought-provoking reflections on art. Excerpts from the novel will be accompanied by classical music that reflects 18th century Italy. Explore the romantic landscapes of Italy to the crystalline harp of Antoine Malette-Chénier, winner of the 2013 OSM Competition."
      }
