    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<p>Led by its gifted conductor Klaus Mäkelä, the Orchestre de Paris will accompany young prodigy Yunchan Lim in Rachmaninoff&rsquo;s celebrated Piano Concerto no. 2. Lim&rsquo;s performance will be preceded and followed by two works heralding the great aesthetic changes of the 20th century: Debussy&rsquo;s <em>Prelude to the Afternoon of a Faun</em>, rich in melodic inventiveness and mesmerizing colours, and Stravinsky&rsquo;s <em>Firebird</em>, whose orchestral splendour rivals with rhythmic audacity.</p>\n"
