    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<p>From Rossini’s celebration of the Swiss Alps to Debussy’s vivid depiction of turbulent waters and Goulet’s Ice Storm, each work on this program draws on natural phenomena to represent Nature’s many facets. The magnificent voice of tenor Pene Pati will bring even more intensity to this concert with arias from Puccini. Reconnect with or discover the OSM under the stars for a spectacular evening of music, nature, and deep emotion.</p>\n"
