        "@value": "<p>López’s symphonic poem <em>Aino</em> is a beautiful tribute to Finland, while Dvořák affirms his Slavic identity in his <em>Symphony No. 6</em> by using material from a Slavic folk dance for the first time. Finally, let yourself be enchanted by Brahms’ legendary <em>Violin Concerto</em>, a mainstay of the instrument’s repertoire, which will be masterfully performed by the internationally acclaimed violinist James Ehnes.</p>\n"
