    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<p>Barbara Hannigan has some exciting surprises lined up for you in this edition of the Concerts éclatés series. Prepare for a vibrant and unforgettable evening where music and dance take centre stage, featuring works by Offenbach, Weill, Glenn Miller, and other carefully curated selections chosen by the conductor herself.</p>\n<p>Barbara Hannigan and Marie-Nicole Lemieux have some exciting surprises lined up for you in this edition of the Concerts éclatés series. Come join the party where music, theme decorations and dance (tango, waltz and foxtrot) take centre stage, featuring works by Offenbach, Weill, Glenn Miller, and other carefully curated selections chosen by the conductor herself.</p>\n<p>What to expect:<br />\n&#8211; 7:30 p.m. to 8 p.m.: Free dance lessons at the Antonia-Nantel Foyer with professional dancers (tango, waltz and foxtrot).<br />\n&#8211; 8:30 p.m.: Concert.<br />\n&#8211; 9:45 p.m. to 11 p.m.: Dance performances and open dance floor with music and animation for a fun-filled evening!</p>\n<p>A free cocktail will also be offered at the bars of the Maison symphonique after the concert, courtesy of Distillerie de Montréal. Quantities are limited, first come, first served! Cheers!</p>\n"
