    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<p>Clarinetist Kinan Azmeh captivates audiences with his fluid, nuanced playing and remarkable improvisational talent. Joined by the OSM and flutist Timothy Hutchins, he will showcase a program that blends creative freedom, Bartók’s folk-inspired motifs, and Carl Philipp Emanuel Bach’s innovative sensitivity. The evening concludes with Mozart’s graceful and elegant <em>Symphony No. 39</em>.</p>\n<p>Coffee is offered courtesy of our Symphonic Matinees presenter, Chartwell, as soon as the doors open.</p>\n"
      }
    ]
  },
