    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "The OSM Carnival – School Matinees"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<p>Reccomended for all elementary school levels</p>\n<p>Presented in French</p>\n<p>In this one-of-a-kind concert, let’s learn about the orchestra and insects without fear! Discover <em>The Carnival of the Insects</em>, a recent work by Quebec composer Maxime Goulet. Each short movement highlights an insect and an orchestra instrument that will have the chance to be heard as a soloist. Ants, bees, beetles, and many other insects will be evoked by the timbres of the four instrument families of the orchestra. To complete the celebration, other bugs might just join in!</p>\n<p><em>*The March 26th performance will be a relaxed concert, presented in a format adapted for individuals with special needs. </em></p>\n<p><strong><a href=\"https://www.osm.ca/en/news/the-carnival-of-the-osm-pedagogical-guide/\">See pedagogical guide</a> </strong></p>\n"
      }
    ]
  },
